      "side": 1,
      "message": "IIUC this is going to waste a bunch of fuzzer time with failed attempts to generate attestation keys.  Can we instead have a separate enum that just has `RSA_ATTEST_KEY` and `EC_ATTEST_KEY` arms, something like:\n\n```\n    uint32_t attestAuthSet \u003d dataProvider-\u003eConsumeEnum\u003cAttestAuthSet\u003e();\n    ....\n    switch (attestAuthSet) {\n        case RSA_ATTEST_KEY: {\n            PaddingMode padding \u003d dataProvider-\u003ePickValueInArray(kPaddingMode);        \n            return AuthorizationSetBuilder()\n                    .Authorization(TAG_NO_AUTH_REQUIRED)\n                    .RsaKey(kRsaKeySize, kPublicExponent)\n                    .Digest(digest)\n                    .Padding(padding)\n                    .AttestKey()\n                    .AttestationChallenge(challenge)\n                    .AttestationApplicationId(id)\n                    .SetDefaultValidity()\n                    .Authorization(TAG_CREATION_DATETIME, timestamp)\n                    .Authorization(TAG_INCLUDE_UNIQUE_ID);\n        } break;\n        case ECDSA_ATTEST_KEY: {\n            EcCurve ecCurve \u003d dataProvider-\u003ePickValueInArray(kCurve);\n            return AuthorizationSetBuilder()\n                    .Authorization(TAG_NO_AUTH_REQUIRED)\n                    .EcdsaKey(ecCurve)\n                    .AttestKey()\n                    .Digest(digest)\n                    .AttestationChallenge(challenge)\n                    .AttestationApplicationId(id)\n                    .SetDefaultValidity()\n                    .Authorization(TAG_CREATION_DATETIME, timestamp)\n                    .Authorization(TAG_INCLUDE_UNIQUE_ID);\n        } break;\n        default: { // unreachable\n            return AuthorizationSetBuilder();\n        } break;\n    }\n\n```",
